{:adr-id "2608300000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-2731 — Fibre Optic Cable Manufacturing Plant Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 2731 (Manufacture of fibre optic cables) had no prior actor
  implementation -- confirmed via gh api 404 that
  github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-2731 did not exist. Per
  this batch's mandatory pre-work verification discipline, the assigned
  slot was independently re-verified against a fresh
  kotoba-lang/industry registry.edn fetch (GitHub Contents API, never
  the raw.githubusercontent.com CDN): {:id \"2731\" :name \"Manufacture
  of fibre optic cables\" :maturity :spec ...}, distinct from sibling
  2732 (\"Manufacture of other electronic and electric wires and
  cables\") and 2733 (\"Manufacture of wiring devices\"), both already
  :implemented in this fleet. No mismatch found; :name was not
  truncated. Fresh, from-scratch scaffold, built as part of a smaller,
  carefully verified batch after an earlier 18-agent haiku batch's 61%
  defect rate -- 120+ consecutive agents on the current stricter
  protocol succeeded before this one. Module shape mirrors sibling
  cloud-itonami-isic-2733 (Manufacture of wiring devices)'s verified
  module shape, domain-adapted for fibre-optic-cable manufacturing:
  fibre drawing (pulling glass fibre from a heated preform on a draw
  tower, with in-line primary/secondary UV-cured acrylate coating)
  followed by cabling (stranding coated fibres into buffer tubes or
  ribbons and jacketing/extruding the finished cable)."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-production-batch, schedule-maintenance,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment. A
   proposal touching drawing/coating/cabling-line-equipment control is
   a hard, permanent block, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Twelve concrete governor checks elaborating four HARD invariants:
   (1) plant/batch record (equipment for maintenance, batch for
   shipment) must be independently verified/registered before any
   action is taken against it, never trusted from the advisor's own
   report, including an independent recompute of shipment quantity
   against the batch's own logged production quantity; (2) the
   request's own :effect must be :propose only; (3) direct
   drawing/coating/cabling-line-equipment control -- including a
   direct :actuate-equipment? true actuation attempt -- is a HARD,
   PERMANENT, unconditional block, no phase and no human override; a
   fifth permanent block (mirroring 2733's own certification-authority
   block) rejects any proposal declaring :issue-certification? true --
   this actor never self-issues a fibre-optic-cable compliance mark
   (Telcordia GR-20 / ITU-T G.65x / UL-NFPA fire-rating); (4) the op
   allowlist is closed to the four ops above. Escalation (soft, human
   may approve): flag-safety-concern always, low confidence (<0.6).
   fibreopticmfg.phase independently agrees -- schedule-maintenance,
   flag-safety-concern, and coordinate-shipment never auto-commit at
   any phase; only log-production-batch may auto-commit, and only at
   phase 3 when governor-clean."
  :module-shape
  "fibreopticmfg.store (MemStore, seeded with a verified/registered
   loose-tube batch with shipping headroom, a verified/registered
   ribbon batch near its shipped-quantity ceiling, an unverified
   tight-buffered batch, a verified/registered fibre-draw-tower unit,
   and an unverified cabling-line unit), fibreopticmfg.registry
   (self-contained pure-function domain logic -- no pre-existing
   kotoba-lang/fibreopticmfg-style capability library to wrap, verified
   none exists), fibreopticmfg.advisor (FibreOpticCableAdvisor, mock +
   real-LLM seam via langchain.model), fibreopticmfg.governor (Fibre
   Optic Cable Plant Operations Governor), fibreopticmfg.phase (0->3
   rollout), fibreopticmfg.operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph),
   fibreopticmfg.sim (demo driver exercising the happy path and all
   eleven HARD-hold scenarios directly)."}
